      <h1>System Architecture</h1>
      <p>The platform follows a microservices architecture with clear separation of concerns.</p>

      <h2>Service Interaction</h2>
      <div class="docs-diagram">
        <div class="mermaid">
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant UI as UI Console
    participant A as Agent Service
    participant LLM as LLM Provider
    participant T as Tools Service
    participant KB as ChromaDB
    participant M as SQLite

    U->>UI: Submit prompt
    UI->>A: POST /agent/run (SSE)
    A->>M: Load conversation history
    A->>KB: RAG retrieval (if relevant)
    A->>LLM: Generate response
    LLM-->>A: Stream tokens
    A->>T: Execute tool calls
    T-->>A: Tool results
    A->>LLM: Continue with tool results
    LLM-->>A: Final response
    A->>M: Save to memory
    A-->>UI: SSE stream
    UI-->>U: Rendered response
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Directory Structure</h2>
      <pre><code>agentic-platform/
├── services/
│   ├── agent/          # Python FastAPI agent service
│   │   ├── agent/      # Core agent modules
│   │   │   ├── graph.py        # LangGraph ReAct agent
│   │   │   ├── llm.py          # Multi-provider LLM factory
│   │   │   ├── memory.py       # SQLite STM + LTM
│   │   │   ├── tools.py        # Tool definitions
│   │   │   ├── vectorstore.py  # ChromaDB integration
│   │   │   └── observability.py # OTel + Langfuse
│   │   └── main.py     # FastAPI app & routes
│   ├── tools/           # External tools microservice
│   ├── ui-console/      # Express.js dashboard
│   └── otel/            # OpenTelemetry collector config
├── n8n/workflows/       # n8n workflow definitions
├── observability/       # Grafana, Prometheus, Loki configs
├── tests/               # Unit, integration, e2e, load tests
├── docs/                # Generated documentation
└── docker-compose.yml   # 13-service orchestration</code></pre>
