    <!-- ── Data Flow ── -->
    <div id="doc-dataflow" class="docs-section">
      <div class="docs-breadcrumb"><a href="/docs">Docs</a> / Architecture</div>
      <h1>Data Flow</h1>
      <p>How data moves through the platform during an agent interaction.</p>

      <h2>Request Lifecycle</h2>
      <div class="docs-diagram">
        <div class="mermaid">
flowchart LR
    A[User Prompt] --> B{Input Guardrails}
    B -->|Pass| C[Load Memory]
    B -->|Block| X[Return Error]
    C --> D[RAG Retrieval]
    D --> E[LLM Inference]
    E --> F{Tool Call?}
    F -->|Yes| G[Execute Tool]
    G --> E
    F -->|No| H{Output Guardrails}
    H -->|Pass| I[Stream Response]
    H -->|Flag| I
    I --> J[Save to Memory]
    J --> K[Emit Telemetry]
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Memory Architecture</h2>
      <p>The platform uses a dual-layer memory system:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Short-Term Memory (STM):</strong> Last 100 messages per session, stored in the <code>conversations</code> table</li>
        <li><strong>Long-Term Memory (LTM):</strong> Rolling 2KB summaries per session in <code>session_summaries</code> table</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="docs-callout info">
        Memory is SQLite-based and lives on a Docker volume. No vector/semantic memory for conversations — that's reserved for the Knowledge Base (ChromaDB).
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Agent System ── -->
    <div id="doc-agents" class="docs-section">
      <div class="docs-breadcrumb"><a href="/docs">Docs</a> / Core Features</div>
      <h1>Agent System</h1>
      <p>The agent system uses the ReAct (Reasoning + Acting) pattern via LangGraph.</p>

      <h2>Agent Lifecycle</h2>
      <div class="docs-diagram">
        <div class="mermaid">
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Receive: User prompt
    Receive --> InputGuardrails: Check safety
    InputGuardrails --> LoadContext: Pass
    InputGuardrails --> Blocked: Block
    LoadContext --> Reason: Memory + RAG
    Reason --> Act: Tool needed
    Act --> Observe: Tool result
    Observe --> Reason: Continue
    Reason --> OutputGuardrails: Final answer
    OutputGuardrails --> Respond: Pass/Flag
    Respond --> SaveMemory
    SaveMemory --> [*]
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Creating Agents</h2>
      <p>Use the <strong>Agent Builder</strong> page to create custom agents with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Custom system prompts</li>
        <li>Tool selection (from registered tools)</li>
        <li>LLM provider and model configuration</li>
        <li>Memory settings</li>
        <li>Guardrail profiles</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Agent-to-Agent (A2A)</h2>
      <p>Agents can delegate tasks to other agents using the A2A protocol. Configure delegation rules on the A2A page.</p>
    </div>

